  "id": "COMPOUND:7940 - PROTEIN:366",
  "verbalization": "Diosmin appears to interact with Betaine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in the methylation of homocysteine. The evidence suggests that Diosmin acts as a target of multiple compounds, including Serine--tRNA ligase, which is itself a target of other molecules. This implies a potential pathway where Diosmin may influence the activity of these enzymes, possibly through competitive inhibition or modulation of their function. The presence of multiple distinct molecular entities acting as intermediaries between Diosmin and the target enzyme suggests a complex network of interactions, possibly involving different mechanisms of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Serine--tRNA ligase in mediating the effect of Diosmin on Betaine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase 1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
